From 155cb29ace55c60d000fc2489349f68b5744062f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:50:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] Round 4: Charge unmonitored Moran row visits in bulk

Without a deadline or cancel file, the work limit is the only possible
stop, so charge all states x (updates + 1) logical row visits with one
Work::advance before the recurrence and drop the per-row step from the
inner loop. Status, detail and step counts are unchanged; a candidate
that exceeds its budget now stops before computing. Monitored budgets
keep interleaved per-row checks. A unit test compares unmonitored and
monitored records at limits around every row boundary.

Workload: lean domain (48 Moran cases, scores on both sides), 11
samples.
Before median: 3.292 ms. After median: 3.051 ms. Speedup: 1.08x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
